  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "HashMgr::free_flag",
    "file": "hunspell/src/hunspell/hashmgr.cxx",
    "description": "`free_flag()` infers ownership from attacker-controlled flag contents: when an AF alias table exists it normally must not free an hentry's shared `astr`, but it does free it if `TESTAFF(astr, ONLYUPCASEFLAG, alen)` succeeds. A malicious alias containing the internal value `ONLYUPCASEFLAG` (65511 / bytes `0xff 0xe7` in `FLAG long` mode) is therefore mistaken for a separately allocated hidden-capitalization flag vector. `free_table()` deletes the shared alias through the dictionary hentry, and `HashMgr::~HashMgr()` subsequently deletes the same allocation from `aliasf`, causing the double-free. Ownership must not be decided from flag values; alternatively reserved internal flags must be rejected from aliases before this state is created.",
    "conditions": "The harness consumes the first byte as a word length, writes that word, and splits all remaining bytes equally into the `.aff` and `.dic` files. The PoV's affix half selects `FLAG long`, declares an `AF` alias table, and makes alias 1 contain `0xffe7`, exactly `ONLYUPCASEFLAG`. The dictionary half has a valid positive count and a dictionary entry using `/1`; `get_aliasf()` stores the shared `aliasf[0]` pointer in that hentry. On object destruction, the presence of the reserved flag makes `free_flag()` free this shared pointer during `free_table()`, after which the alias-table destructor loop frees it again."
  },
